<title>USA: American Express Q4 shr rises.</title>
<headline>American Express Q4 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr primary     $1.23		    $0.77</p>
<p> Net		 595,000		  384,000</p>
<p> Revs		4,257,000		4,048,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  482,065,000	    493,326,000</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr primary     $3.90		    $3.11</p>
<p> Net		 1,901,000		1,564,000</p>
<p> Revs		16,237,000	     15,841,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  485,595,000	    497,953,000</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Full company name is American Express Co.  </p>
<p>1996 year and quarterly per share figures include $300 million after-tax gain on the exchange of the company's Debt Exchangeable for Common Stock for shares of common stock of First Data Corp and a $138 million restructuring after-tax charge.</p>
<p>Before the gain and charge, operating income for the quarter was $433 million or $0.90 a share, compared to $384 million and $0.77. It was $1.7 billion or $3.57 a share for the year against $1.6 billion and $3.11.</p>
<p>First Call's analysts' mean estimate for the fourth quarter was $0.89 a share.</p>
</text>
